  "_comment": "Single source of truth for the industry benchmarks that anchor pre-audit opportunity sizing and 2 of the 5 score dimensions. Refresh quarterly via WebSearch and bump `refreshed`. Every value MUST carry a source + source_date so the report can cite it and a prospect cannot discredit an uncited number. Structure: `global` = flat cross-vertical fallbacks; `verticals` = per-vertical observed metrics; `geos` = per-country CPM with an index relative to the US. There is NO observed vertical-by-geo cell in any public source we have — a vertical figure shown for a non-US market is DERIVED (vertical value x geo CPM index) and must be labeled as such by benchmarks.py resolve(). Never render a derived or global number as if it were measured for the prospect's vertical and country.",
